WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.240
Around 1233, in Montpellier
in southern France,

2
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.310
copies of famous Jewish books were burned.

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.610
Their author was Maimonides.

4
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.920
Some rabbis in Provence
had banned his writings.

5
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.930
Yet today his principles of faith
are sung in the hymn Yigdal,

6
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.440
and printed in Orthodox prayer books.

7
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:24.250
If his list is so loved, why did
other great rabbis argue with it?

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.000
In this mission, you'll
explore principles 6 to 13:

9
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:33.770
prophecy, Moses, the Torah, reward,
the Messiah and resurrection.

10
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.120
Then you'll follow the arguments
from his own lifetime to today,

11
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.870
and see where Jewish movements differ.

12
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.830
Your mission: find out why other great
rabbis argued with Maimonides' list.
